      "worked": "The line $2x-4y-7=0$ has gradient $\\dfrac12$. The perpendicular normal gradient is $-2$, so the tangent gradient is $\\dfrac12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+3}}\\\\\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+3}}&=\\dfrac12\\\\\\sqrt{2x+3}&=2\\\\2x+3&=4\\\\x&=\\dfrac12.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt $x=\\dfrac12$, $y=2$. Hence,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-2&=-2\\left(x-\\dfrac12\\right)\\\\y&=-2x+3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
